Dear DGAC team,


Thank you for your message.


I must express my surprise at your statement that you do not have access to
the materials I sent, given that the full documentation was properly
delivered via email on *31 October 2025* to multiple DGAC officials,
including this address, and confirmed as sent with valid access links.


All files were shared through secure Google Drive links, and any recipient
listed in the email =E2=80=94 or any authorized DGAC account =E2=80=94 may =
access them
simply by clicking the links or requesting access if needed. Please specify
which link or file you are unable to open so that I may verify the
technical issue on your side.


As clearly stated in my previous message, I requested confirmation of
receipt *and clarification on how your institution intends to proceed* in
light of the documentation provided. To date, neither has been addressed.


I am, once again, acting in good faith and willing to re-submit the
material if strictly necessary. However, it is essential that this time
your office ensures the proper registration, acknowledgment, and internal
circulation of my submission.


Please confirm by return email:


   1.

   Which specific files or links you cannot access.
   2.

   The official case or tracking number assigned to my submission.
   3.

   How and when the DGAC intends to review or respond to the contents
   provided.


I look forward to your prompt and substantive response.


Kind regards,

*Leandro Disconzi*

